-- title:
--   Tame supersingular node: widehat𝒪≅ W[[U,V]]/(UV-varpiᵖ⁻¹)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and an integer $M\neq 0$ with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$, subject to two tameness conditions: either $p\neq2$ or some prime $\ell\mid M$ has $\ell\not\equiv1\pmod 4$, and if $p=3$ then some prime $\ell\mid M$ has $\ell\not\equiv1\pmod 3$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_1$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L142) of $\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of that rational function field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A\to L$, and acting on $K_1$ compatibly with $L$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j\in K_1$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Consider $\mathcal Y=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K₁ j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements of $K_1$ integral over $A[j]$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the algebra of elements integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $z$ be a point of $\mathcal Y$ and $\varpi_z$ the germ at $z$ of the global function pulled back from $\varpi$, assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathcal Y,z}$ (so $z$ lies over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$). Let $y$ be a point of the finite chart $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K₁ j` mapping to $z$ under `ιFin`, and assume $y$ is supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K₁ j` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$ for which every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $p$-torsion point. Then there exist a discrete valuation domain $W$ that is complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, a ring homomorphism $\sigma\colon A\to W$ such that $\sigma\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal of $W$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathcal Y,z}$ along its maximal ideal onto [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel W ((σ ϖ)^(p-1))`](def/ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel.html#L15), the quotient of the power series ring in two variables over $W$ by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal W ((σ ϖ)^(p-1))`, such that for every $a\in A$ the element of the completion coming from the germ at $z$ of the pullback of $a$ is carried by $e$ to the constant $\sigma a$.
--
--   This is the local structure of the integral model of $X(\Gamma_1(M)\cap\Gamma_0(p))$ over a ramified base at a supersingular point of the characteristic-$p$ fibre: the completed local ring is a crossing of thickness $p-1$ over an unramified extension $W$ of $A$, in the spirit of the Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur descriptions of the supersingular points of $\Gamma_0(p)$-level curves, here under a tameness condition on the auxiliary level $M$. It feeds the corresponding statement for the model of $X_1(Mp)$.
